ker is strong, I lose to any Ace (A-x makes 5-5-5-A-J), any pocket pair, or any 4/J. If I bet, hands worse than mine (like Q-high) will almost certainly fold, so I extract no value. Conversely, hands better than mine (like A-high or a low pocket pair) might call or raise. Therefore, betting has no upside (value) and only downside (risk). Checking back is the optimal play to realize my showdown value and win the pot against the opponent's weak range without risking additional chips.\n\nReason: My hand has decent showdown value (Trips with King kicker) but is vulnerable to better kickers or full houses. Given the opponent's passivity, checking is the best way to win the pot against their air/weak range, as betting will likely only be called by hands that beat me.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
